# Supabase Migration SQL (project deltas)

General Postgres and Supabase SQL patterns: [Supabase database overview](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview). Migration **process and safety** (one file per change, no push): `do-migrations-agent.mdc`. App-level security workflow: `security.mdc` and `supabase.mdc`.

## Style

- Write SQL in **lowercase** with consistent indentation.
- **snake_case** for tables and columns; **plural** table names.
- Default primary key: `id bigint generated always as identity primary key` unless the table is 1:1 with `auth.users` (then `id uuid` FK to `auth.users(id)` — see profiles migration).
- Always qualify schema (`public.profiles`, not bare `profiles`).
- Add a `comment on table` describing purpose (up to 1024 chars).
- Header comment block per migration: purpose, affected objects, RLS summary.

**Canonical shipped example:** [`supabase/migrations/20260622120000_create_profiles.sql`](../../supabase/migrations/20260622120000_create_profiles.sql)

## Row Level Security

Enable RLS on every new table — no exceptions. See [Supabase RLS docs](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/row-level-security) for general policy syntax.

### Owner-scoped pattern (default for user data)

Use `(select auth.uid()) = id` (or the owning column) in policy clauses. Canonical reference: [`20260622120000_create_profiles.sql`](../../supabase/migrations/20260622120000_create_profiles.sql).

| Operation | Clause shape |
| --------- | ------------ |
| SELECT | `using` only |
| INSERT | `with check` only |
| UPDATE | `using` and `with check` |
| DELETE | `using` only |

- One policy per operation — never `for all`.
- Always specify role with `to authenticated` (or `anon` when intentionally public).
- Policies are **PERMISSIVE** by default. `as restrictive` is a **rare documented exception** only (e.g. MFA enforcement via `auth.jwt()->>'aal'`); do not use restrictive policies for routine owner checks.
- Wrap `auth.uid()` and `auth.jwt()` in `(select …)` for planner caching — see [RLS performance](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/row-level-security#rls-performance-recommendations).
- Index columns referenced in policy `using` / `with check` clauses.

Storage bucket policies follow the same owner pattern via `(storage.foldername(name))[1] = (select auth.uid())::text` — see [`20260623120000_create_avatars_bucket.sql`](../../supabase/migrations/20260623120000_create_avatars_bucket.sql).

## Database functions

Project conventions beyond Supabase defaults:

- Default **`security invoker`**; use **`security definer`** only when required (e.g. signup trigger writing across schemas) and document why.
- Always **`set search_path = ''`** and use fully qualified object names inside the function body.
- Trigger functions: `returns trigger`, `language plpgsql`, attach with explicit `create trigger … execute function`.

**Canonical shipped example:** `handle_new_user()` in [`20260622120000_create_profiles.sql`](../../supabase/migrations/20260622120000_create_profiles.sql). General function patterns: [Supabase database functions](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/functions).

